From 0a0281f3c4470365999607aa76342eebf06551d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Barnard <kevin.barnard@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 02:41:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] [minixrs] Driver: add the MinixRS toolchain

Give aarch64-unknown-minixrs a real toolchain instead of letting it fall
through to Generic_ELF, which drove /usr/bin/gcc as the linker.

Shaped after Fuchsia -- derives from ToolChain directly, so none of the
GCC-detection machinery in Generic_ELF applies. Behaviour is fixed by the
tooling repo's docs/sysroot-layout.md, not invented here:

  - ld.lld is the linker (getDefaultLinker, and the driver dir is on the
    program paths, so the SDK's own lld is found).
  - -static unconditionally. The platform has no shared objects and no
    dynamic linker, so there is no -shared/-pie path to select between.
  - -z max-page-size=4096 -z separate-loadable-segments, which is what the
    minixrs loader requires of every PT_LOAD (D13).
  - crt1.o/crti.o ... crtn.o and -L out of <sysroot>/usr/lib, headers out
    of <sysroot>/usr/include.
  - compiler-rt builtins; libc++ if C++ ever arrives; no sanitizers.

The sysroot is computed relative to the driver binary (<driver dir>/../
sysroot) rather than baked in via DEFAULT_SYSROOT, because only the
$MINIXRS_SDK prefix is contractual and the SDK has to stay relocatable.
The dots are folded out so the crt and -L paths that reach the link line
are canonical sysroot paths.

tooling/verify/check-driver.sh now passes all three steps (its crt/sysroot
assertions still SKIP -- the sysroot itself arrives in P3).
